# Fork versioning guard.
#
# This fork (JoseLuckmann/hivemind) cuts its own releases with a "-flow" pre-release
# suffix (e.g. 1.16.0-flow.1). The release process edits the `version` field in every
# package.json and prepends a section to CHANGELOG.md — the exact same lines upstream
# (dip497/hivemind) also edits on every one of its releases.
#
# Left alone, `git merge upstream/main` would collide on these files on EVERY upstream
# release, forever. The `merge=ours` driver tells git to KEEP OUR version of these files
# during a merge, dropping the incoming upstream change for them only. All other files
# (the actual code) merge normally, so we still get upstream's features — we just keep
# our own version numbers and changelog.
#
# NOTE: `merge=ours` requires the driver to be registered locally (it is not stored in
# the repo). Run once per clone:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# (the installer/release flow does this; see scripts/release.sh header).

CHANGELOG.md      merge=ours
package.json      merge=ours
**/package.json   merge=ours
